content.text:
Let's ensure that when `api_citation_handler` and `api_arrest_handler` succeed in sending to Discord, they ALSO add a record to `records_list` so that citations and arrests logged anywhere (including via the main page / utilities panel / Logs and BOLOs / Discord commands) update to the utilities panel and records feed!
Wait, let's check what fields `new_record` needs:
```python
        new_record = {
            "id": int(time.time() * 1000),
            "type": "citation", # or "arrest"
            "plate": data.get("plate", "UNKNOWN").upper()[:10] if isinstance(data, dict) else "UNKNOWN",
            "vehicle": data.get("vehicle", "Unknown") if isinstance(data, dict) else "Unknown",
            "subject": suspect,
            "secondary": reason,
            "description": f"Court date: {court_date}" if "court_date" in locals() else f"Arrest reason: {reason}",
            "timestamp": time.time() * 1000
        }
        records_list.insert(0, new_record)
        save_shift_data()
```
And on the frontend (`panel-frontend.html`), when submitting a citation or arrest in Logs and BOLOs (`submitNewLog`), if `currentLogFormType === 'citation'`, it should post to `/api/citation` (or use the main page form submission logic); if `currentLogFormType === 'arrest'`, it should post to `/api/arrest`.
Wait, let's re-read the user instructions:
"On the website, make the citation log in Logs and BOLOs update to utilities panel."
"That's what I's saying. I need it to connect to the main page, and to the Discord, but NOT the examples."
"Also, make sure all of them are the same other then citation logging and arrest logging, make it go though the main page one (Utilities Panel)"

This means:
1. When submitting a **citation** log or **arrest** log from Logs and BOLOs, it should use the exact same logic/endpoint as the main page (Utilities Panel) — i.e., posting to `/api/citation` or `/api/arrest` (which sends to Discord AND creates a record so it updates the utilities panel/records).
2. Other log types (BOLOs, Vehicle Notes) continue using `/api/records`.
3. Remove all example records (EXAMPLE BOLO) from both code and stored records (`records.json`).

Let's check `panel-frontend.html` `submitNewLog`:
```javascript
      async function submitNewLog(event) {
        event.preventDefault();
        const plate = document.getElementById('log-plate').value.trim().toUpperCase().slice(0, 10);
        const vehicle = document.getElementById('log-vehicle').value.trim();
        const subject = document.getElementById('log-subject').value.trim() || 'Unknown';
        const secondary = document.getElementById('log-secondary').value.trim() || 'General';
        const description = document.getElementById('log-description').value.trim();

        if (!plate || !description) {
          showNotification('Please fill in plate and description.', 'error');
          return;
        }

        if (currentLogFormType === 'citation') {
          // Route through main page citation logging (/api/citation)
          const formData = new FormData();
          formData.append('user', subject);
          formData.append('reason', `${secondary} - ${description}`);
          formData.append('court_date', 'Not scheduled');

          try {
            const res = await fetch('/api/citation', {
              method: 'POST',
              body: formData
            });
            const resData = await res.json();
            if (res.ok) {
              showNotification('Citation record submitted to Discord and updated to utilities panel successfully!', 'success');
              document.getElementById('new-log-form').reset();
              setLogFormType(currentLogFormType);
              fetchRecords(); // Refresh records feed
            } else {
              showNotification(resData.error || 'Failed to submit citation log', 'error');
            }
          } catch (e) {
            showNotification('Network error submitting citation log', 'error');
          }
          return;
        }

        if (currentLogFormType === 'arrest') {
          // Route through main page arrest logging (/api/arrest)
          const formData = new FormData();
          formData.append('user', subject);
          formData.append('reason', `${secondary} - ${description}`);

          try {
            const res = await fetch('/api/arrest', {
              method: 'POST',
              body: formData
